{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And of Zion</b> — 'and for the sake of Zion.' The lamed: my brother said to me, it always says איש ואיש נולד בה, for the sages who have a name are many." "<b>And the meaning of איש ואיש</b> — not this one alone." "<b>He establishes it</b> — in the manner of 'and He commanded' [referring to הוא יאמר תמיד איש ואיש נולד בה above], and 'and He, the Most High, establishes it' — because HaShem is in the force of the verbs, and its meaning is the Name mentioned above: 'YHWH loves the gates of Zion.'" "<b>He establishes it</b> — the Foundation of the Most High. And the meaning: such a place where many sages are born there — HaShem will establish it and firmly found it."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 87, :notes {0 "The Hebrew להלמ\"ד is obscure; read as ל-ה\"ל-מ\"ד (concerning the lamed). The phrase אמרי לי אחי is unusual word order."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:36:16.824955936Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}